{
  "pedal": "Boss AW-3 Dynamic Wah — a check at settings in no fit: guitar excerpts over a quiet comb of tones (mono: Guitar input -> Output)",
  "comment": "A short session to look for any large difference between the pedal and NAM-X's Wah where nothing was fitted: four knob settings (two at the end stops, two in between), each in Up, Down and Sharp. Never fit on it. Each take plays stabs, funk and dynamics from the guitar DI dataset (captures/di/) over five steady sines (331 Hz to 2971 Hz, each 50 dB under the guitar's peak), as the focused session of 2026-11-11 did: the filter's place over time is read on the tones between hits and on the guitar while it plays. The knobs are frozen per block of three takes; only Mode turns inside a block, and it stays where it is from one block to the next. Clock positions: 7:00 = fully counter-clockwise, 5:00 = fully clockwise.",
  "quiet_dbfs": -60,
  "knobs": [
    "Mode",
    "Manual",
    "Sens",
    "Decay"
  ],
  "takes": [
    {
      "name": "bypass-funk",
      "bypass": true,
      "signal": {
        "type": "file",
        "path": "captures/di/funk.wav",
        "seconds": 12,
        "probe": {
          "freq": [
            331,
            577,
            997,
            1723,
            2971
          ],
          "level_db": -50
        },
        "tail": 1.0
      },
      "note": "The pedal off (its LED off): the reference. Interface out 3 to Guitar input, Output to interface input 2, nothing in EXP/CTL, the 9 V adapter. The short patch cable back between interface out 4 and input 5."
    },
